From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 15:00:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: h713: give the console UART its pins

uart0_ph_pins (PH0/PH1, 10 mA, pull-up) was defined but the console
UART did not reference it, so the pins kept whatever the bootloader set.
Reference it. U-Boot, moving to this device tree, applied exactly this
group from its own tree, so neither side's pin state changes.

Signed-off-by: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
@@ -716,6 +716,8 @@
 			clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_UART0>;
 			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_UART0>;
 			clock-frequency = <24000000>;
+			pinctrl-names = "default";
+			pinctrl-0 = <&uart0_ph_pins>;
 			status = "okay";
 		};
 
